**FX reversal**: Weak dollar adds ~1.5pts of revenue growth in FY26. With DXY at 98.9 near multi-year lows, the tailwind is at its maximum \u2014 mean-reversion of the dollar wipes out 1-2pts of growth and embarrasses the guidance.\n6. **Share count illusion**: 903M diluted shares \u2192 878M = 2.8% shrink in one year; EPS growth of 15% is ~12% operational + 3% buyback. Buyback at 30x P/E is value-destructive math, whatever management says about \"long-term conviction\".\n7. **Geopolitical recurrences**: Q2'26 already hit cross-border. Spikes in Middle East conflicts are persistent and unforecastable (currently 6% of cross-border volume at risk).\n\n**Step 9-2. Logic Combat**\n- Long logic strength: 7/10 (quality, duopoly, cash generation, management discipline)\n- Short logic strength: 6/10 (regulatory binary, valuation, VAS margin math)\n- Gap = 1 <2 \u2192 **No conviction downgrade. Expected value negative at current price stands.**\n\n**Step 9-3. Adversarial Data**\n- No active Hindenburg-style report on MA. The relevant activist evidence is:\n  - Court-approved $5.5B settlement (partial distributions Feb 2026) [Actual]\n  - CCCA reintroduced Jan 2026, new co-sponsors [Actual - gooden.house.gov]\n  - UK court loss re cross-border fee caps [Actual - Bloomberg 1/2026]\n\n**Step 9-4. Killed Arguments**\n1. \"Stablecoins will destroy card networks in 5 years\" \u2192 KILLED (for now): incumbent banks and networks are adopting stablecoin rails; the card network standards may survive as the interface. Condition to revive: if a top-3 U.S. issuer launches a merchant-direct A2A settlement product at scale with consumer rewards.\n2. \"E-wallets (24.9% share) are taking share\" \u2192 KILLED (for now): wallets sit ON TOP of card networks (Apple Pay, Google Pay tokenize MA/Visa cards); MA still earns network fees.\n3. \"MA has no net cash\" \u2192 KILLED as a bear point: 0.46x net debt/EBITDA is trivial; credit rating AA; interest coverage 27.8x.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500