x compression sits ahead.\n- Regulatory tail risk (CCCA) and political fee pressure are live, not hypothetical: the $5.5B settlement was just court-approved in June 2026.\n- Expected 3-year total return from T0: +3-6%/yr (28x \u00d7 EPS $24.9 = $697 bull; 25x \u00d7 EPS $24.9 = $622 base; that base is +2.3%/yr) \u2014 BELOW the 8.75% opportunity cost.\n\n**Execution plan:**\n| Tranche | Zone | Size | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | $500\u2013520 | 3% | Limit orders resting; any market drawdown to 26x forward |\n| 2 | $460\u2013480 | +2% | 24x forward, or Q3'26 VAS re-acceleration |\n| 3 | $420\u2013460 | +1% (to 6%) | 22x forward \u2014 correlates with either recession or CCCA panic; requires intact margins to deploy |\n| Exit/Trim | >$620 | -1% per +5% | Trim on euphoria; do not hold through a CCCA Senate markup |\n\n**Monitoring cadence:** Quarterly earnings (next Oct 22, 2026); monthly CCCA tracker; weekly 10Y and DXY check. Pre-mortem conditions logged.\n\n**Bottom line:** Mastercard is a magnificent business trading 10% above its intrinsic value with a live regulatory overhang. The risk-reward at $580.63 is asymmetric to the downside. Patience is the position: hold cash or existing shares, place the buy zone at $500, and let the market come to you.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 END OF REPORT \u2014 v2.0 ENGINE SIGN-OFF\n\u25a0 IV: $518 | EV: $529 | MoS: -9.8% | Conviction: 12/15 HIGH\n\u25a0 DISCLOSURE: All forecasts beyond FY2027 rely on [Assumption] and are\n  shown in the model; the CCCA risk is real and binary.\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u255