n  debt \u2212 cash); GAAP ROE \u2248 193% (leveraged by buybacks) [Estimate]\n- FCF margin: 52.3% (OCF\u2212capex basis FY2025); conservative (ex-SBC, software\n  capex) \u2248 45\u201348% [Estimate \u2014 pack + my adjustment]\n- FCF conversion vs NI: 115% [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: LT debt $18.251B + current portion $0.749B \u2212 cash $10.566B =\n  $8.434B; plus operating leases $0.833B \u2192 adjusted net debt ~$9.3B\n  [Arithmetic/Estimate \u2014 components from pack, overlap unverified]\n- Net debt / EBITDA \u2248 9.3 / 20.0 = 0.46x [Estimate]\n- Interest coverage: 18.897 / 0.680 = 27.8x [Arithmetic FY2025]\nJUDGMENT: EXCELLENT.\n\n2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u201315):\n1. Buyback efficiency: 3 \u2014 $5.7B in Q1 + late April 2026 and $4.9B in Q2 +\n   $0.7B July 2026; $14B authorization Dec 2025 [Estimate \u2014 TIKR / Motley Fool;\n   Actual for authorization \u2014 investor.mastercard.com]. Buybacks at $495\u2013$580\n   are below my intrinsic value.\n2. M&A track record: 2 \u2014 VAS tuck-ins (Vocalink, Ethoca, SessionM, Aiia,\n   Recorded Future) are small, strategic, integrated. No large impairments,\n   but the \"5-yr ROIC > WACC +3%\" proof at scale is [Unconfirmed].\n3. Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 $0.49B capex on $17B FCF; marginal ROIC >> 20%.\n4. Rationality of mix: 3 \u2014 reinvest in VAS + steady return of capital.\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 \u2014 Q1'26 and Q2'26 beat; FY26 guidance affirmed/raised.\nTOTAL: 14/15. Insider ownership 0.11%; no bonus. Recent insider buys/sells:\n[Unconfirmed]. Cap-allocation score: 14/15.\n\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS  [Layer 2.5]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500