66 | Sh 772 | FCFE/sh $39.70\nFY35: Rev 64.2 | OM 64.0% | OI 41.1 | NOPAT 32.46 | +D&A 2.25\n  -Capex 1.54 -SBC 1.16 | FCFE 32.01 | Sh 760 | FCFE/sh $42.10\n\nTerminal value at end-FY35:\nFCFE_36 = 32.01 \u00d7 (1 + 0.035) \u00d7 (1 - 0.015 - 0.01) \u2248 $31.0B (after reducing\nshare count at -1.5% and returning 100% FCF; the \"\u00d71.035\" is growth,\nthe reduction reflects future buyback; net effect = 1.035 - 0.025 = 1.01)\n[Assumption\u2014simplified but conservative].\nTerminal FCFE = 32.01 \u00d7 1.01 = $32.3B.\nTV = 32.3 / (0.085 - 0.035) = $646B [Estimate].\nPV of TV = 646 / (1.085)^10 = 646 / 2.261 = $285.7B [Estimate].\nPV of explicit FCFE (discounted at 8.5%):\nFY26: 16.55/1.085 = 15.25\nFY27: 18.62/1.177 = 15.82\nFY28: 20.64/1.277 = 16.16\nFY29: 22.71/1.385 = 16.40\nFY30: 24.48/1.503 = 16.29\nFY31: 26.25/1.630 = 16.10\nFY32: 27.80/1.768 = 15.72\nFY33: 29.24/1.918 = 15.24\nFY34: 30.66/2.080 = 14.74\nFY35: 32.01/2.256 = 14.19\n\u03a3 PV explicit \u2248 $156.0B [Estimate].\nEnterprise value = 156.0 + 285.7 = $441.7B [Estimate].\nAdd: excess cash (cash 10.57 - net debt 8.5 = +2.07) [Estimate\u2014see Layer 6B].\nEquity value = 443.7B [Estimate].\nPer share on 760M FY2035 shares is wrong for T0: use T0 diluted shares 906M\n(the buyback is already embedded in FCFE_sh above, so do not double-count).\nT0 diluted FCFE base already uses declining shares; therefore:\nIV per share at T0 = 443.7B / 0.906B = $489.8B [Correction: numerator must\nexclude the buyback-share benefit already inside FCFE per share; the correct\napproach is to discount *total* FCFE, not FCFE per share, and then divide\nby T0 diluted shares.] \u2190 RECONCILIATION:\nThe per-share FCFE numbers above were derived by applying the buyback\nreduction *to the share count*, but the FCFE figures themselves are *total*\nFCFE-to-equity. Recomputing per-share IV:\nIV = (\u03a3 discounted total FCFE + PV TV) / T0 diluted shares\n= (156.0 + 285.7) / 0.906 = 441.7 / 0.906 = $487.5 [Estimate].\n\nADD BACK: VAS intangible asset value (incremental to DCF) = $40\u201360B\n[Estimate\u2014VAS 40% of revenue with 18% growth and network-agnostic optionality;\nIV uplift ~$55/share].\nAlso add back: Excess capital not in net debt (marketable securities, if\nreinstated) [Unconfirmed\u2014not held]; offset by uncertainty on capex definition\n[Unconfirmed\u2014capitalized software potentially higher].\n\nCONCILIATION:\nDCF Base IV $487.5 + VAS / tax-amortization uplift ~$35\u201355 + net excess cash\n~$2\u20135 = $525\u2013575 [Estimate].\nMidpoint: ~$555 [Estimate].\nHowever, I also anchor with earnings multiple (see below) to sanity check.\n\nMULTIPLES ANCHOR (not the conclusion, only a cross-check):\nFY26E GAAP diluted EPS (using 890M shares) \u2248 16.83 \u00d7 (1-0.205) / 0.890 = ~$15.10\n[Estimate].\nAdjusted EPS (ex-intangibles, adjusted for SBC add-back) \u2248 ~$15.90 [Estimate].\nHistorical 5-yr forward P/E band: 25\u201332 [Estimate\u2014V/MA multi-year band].\nAt 26\u00d7 FY26E GAAP EPS: $393 | At 30\u00d7: $453 | At 33\u00d7: $498 [Estimate].\nMy DCF IV of $488\u2013555 implies ~32\u201336\u00d7 FY26E EPS, above the historical\nband but justified by VAS mix shift and quality score.\n\nBLENDED BASE INTRINSIC VALUE = 50% DCF-equity (post-add-backs) + 30% EV/EBITDA\ncross-check + 20% quality-adjusted multiple [Assumption]:\nDCF midpoint: $525.5\nEV/EBITDA: FY26 EBITDA 22.6, net debt adj 9.1, EV 519; at 23\u00d7 EV/EBITDA\n(quality premium; historical 20\u201324\u00d7) \u2192 $540 [Estimate].\nQuality-adjusted P/E: 30\u00d7 FY26 adj EPS 15.90 = $477 [Estimate].\nBlended Base IV = 0.5\u00d7525.5 + 0.3\u00d7540 + 0.2\u00d7477 = $540.4 [Estimate].\nI round the Base IV to $540 [Estimate] (50% CI $520\u2013$575; 80% CI $480\u2013$620).\nNote: My earlier \"IV $579\" line in Section 0 was the 50th-percentile model\nblend before the capex-deceleration haircut; with the conservative\nrebates/incentives escalation and tax 20.5%, final Base IV is $540.\n\nTornado sensitivity (top 3