\n\u25a0 LAYER 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nRISKS (ranked):\n1. REGULATORY: CCCA/re-routing mandates (currently defeated in NDAA and\n   housing bill, but co-sponsors added [Actual\u2014CardRates & PYMNTS 2026]).\n   Impact: -15% to -25% IV in Bear. Watch: committee votes, House floor.\n2. MACRO/CREDIT: U.S. consumer delinquencies rising (web brief; household\n   stress, oil prices) \u2192 GDV deceleration. Impact: -10%.\n3. FX: Strong USD pressures cross-border (20% of revenue). Impact: -3\u20135%.\n4. COMPETITIVE: VAS price wars (Visa, FIS), rebates & incentives +20%\n   [Actual] compress economics. Impact: -5%.\n5. CONCENTRATION: Top 10 issuers (large banks) renegotiate / co-op with\n   rivals. Watch for JPM/Chase renewals \u2014 currently renewed [Actual].\n6. TECHNOLOGY: Stablecoins/CBDC disintermediate cross-border;\n   impact long-term, not in 3-yr window.\n\nCATALYSTS:\n\u2022 FY26 EPS beat / guidance raise (Q3'26 and Q4'26 prints).\n\u2022 VAS acceleration >20% CN.\n\u2022 Final court approval of $38B swipe-fee settlement (preliminary OK June 9,\n  2026 [Actual\u2014Reuters]) \u2014 removes legal overhang.\n\u2022 UAE switching deal / Agentic Commerce (Agent Pay for Machines) monetization\n  [Actual\u2014Q2'26 call].\n\u2022 Buyback execution: $14B authorization [Actual\u2014DeepResearchGlobal]; each\n  $1B buyback is ~$1.14 EPS accretive.\n\nStep 7-4. PRE-MORTEM (5 years from now, MA failed):\n1. \"Why did the network lose the rails?\" \u2014 CBDC/stablecoin rails bypassed\n   card networks; cross-border volumes down 40%. Early warning: CBDC pilot\n   scale in EU/China; declining cross-border volume ex-Ven