ngEconomics]\n- ERP: 4.75% [Assumption]\n- Beta: 0.735 [Aggregator \u2014 pack, window unstated]; I use 0.85 [Assumption \u2014\n  forward-leaning beta for consumption-linked payments with stable B2B2C\n  revenues; 0.735 is likely a long-window historical low]\n- Cost of equity = 4.71% + 0.85 \u00d7 4.75% = 8.75% [Estimate]\n- Pre-tax cost of debt \u2248 4.9% (AA-rated, +25bp over 10Y) [Assumption];\n  after-tax = 4.9 \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.18) = 4.02% [Estimate]\n- Weights: E = 509.8 / (509.8+9.3) = 98.2%; D = 1.8% [Estimate]\n- WACC = 8.75 \u00d7 0.982 + 4.02 \u00d7 0.018 = 8.66 \u2192 use 8.6% [Estimate/Assumption]\nNote: this is HIGHER than historical MA analyses because the 10Y is at 4.71%.\n\n3-2. Explicit forecast (FISCAL YEARS, Dec 31-end; $B).\nForecast sources: FY2026E growth = company guide \"high end of low double-digit,\ncurrency-neutral, plus ~1.5pt FX\" [Estimate \u2014 TIKR quoting Q1'26 call; Motley\nFool transcript re Q3'26 guide \"high-end low double digits\"]; Q1'26 + Q2'26\nactuals 8.398 + 9.277 [Actual \u2014 pack]. Years 2\u20135 = fade from ~12% to ~9.7%\n[Assumption \u2014 VAS ~20% growth offsetting network ~8%, linear blend]; Years\n6\u201310 fade to ~7% [Assumption]; terminal 4.0% = long-run nominal GDP\n[Assumption]. Op margin 57.7% \u2192 60.7% (+30bp/yr early, fading to +10bp/yr)\n[Assumption \u2014 scale + pricing, partially offset by VAS mix; Q2'26 op margin\nalready 60.2% per LBank]. Tax + net-interest drag: 20.7% of operating income\n(calibrated to FY2025: 1 \u2212 14.97/18.90) [Arithmetic \u2014 assumption held flat].\nBroad capex = 2.0% of revenue (between filed 1.5% and vendor 3.7%) [Assumption];\nD&A = 3.5% of revenue (FY2025 3.5%) [Estimate]; SBC = 1.8% of revenue (FY2025\n1.8%) [Estimate].\n\nFY     Rev     OpM%   OpInc    NI     D&A   CapX   SBC    FCF(broad)\n2026E  37.40   57.7   21.58   17.11   1.31  0.75  0.67   17.00\n2027E  41.90   58.2   24.39   19.34   1.47  0.84  0.75   19.22\n2028E  46.50   58.6   27.25   21.61   1.63  0.93  0.84   21.47\n2029E  51.30   59.0   30.27   24.00   1.80  1.03  0.92   23.85\n2030E  56.30   59.3   33.39   26.47   1.97  1.13  1.01   26.30\n2031E  61.50   59.6   36.65   29.07   2.15  1.23  1.11   28.88\n2032E  66.90   60.0   40.14   31.83   2.34  1.34  1.20   31.63\n2033E  72.40   60.2   43.58   34.56   2.53  1.45  1.30   34.34\n2034E  77.90   60.5   47.13   37.37   2.73  1.56  1.40   37.14\n2035E  83.40   60.7   50.62   40.15   2.92  1.67  1.50   39.90\n\nTerminal FCF (2036E) = 83.40\u00d71.04 \u00d7 (0.607\u00d70.793 + 0.035 \u2212 0.020 \u2212 0.018)\n= 86.74 \u00d7 0.4784 = 41.50 [Arithmetic on assumptions above]\nTV = 41.50 / (0.086 \u2212 0.04) = 902.2B [Arithmetic]\nTerminal value share of EV = 416.7 / 597.5 = 70% \u2014 HIGH, driven by the\nasset-light model and long growth runway.\n\n3-3. PV calculation (discount at 8.6%; t = 0.35 for FY2026E, then 1.35, 2.35,\n... 9.35; TV at 9.35):\nPV(FY2026E\u2013FY2035E FCF) = 16.52+17.18+17.67+18.07+18.35+18.56+18.71+18.71+\n18.63+18.43 = 180.8B\nPV(TV) = 902.2 \u00d7 0.4619 = 416.7B\nEV = 597.5B\nAdjustments: + cash 10.57 [Actual FY2025; TTM cash [Unconfirmed]]\n\u2212 long-term debt 18.25 \u2212 current portion 0.75 = 19.00 (matches vendor total-debt\nscalar of $19.000B, giving me confidence the components are the total)\n[Arithmetic/Actual]\n\u2212 operating leases 0.83 [Actual]\n+ marketable securities: [Unconfirmed] \u2014 NOT in pack; if they run the typical\nmedian 32% of cash, add ~$3.4B, +$4/share (immaterial to the conclusion).\nEquity value = 597.5 + 10.57 \u2212 19.00 \u2212 0.83 = 588.2B\nIntrinsic value per share = 588.2 / 0.878 = $670 [Estimate]\nMargin of safety = (670 \u2212 580.63) / 670 = 13.3% \u2192 LIMITED\n\n3-4. Parallel multiples cross-check:\n- Trailing P/E: 31.2x [Actual \u2014 market data]. My IV implies 36.2x TTM EPS\n  $18.52, or 31.3x FY2027E EPS ~21.4 \u2014 reasonable for a compounder growing\n  15% with a 45% net margin.\n- EV/Sales: market 13.6x; my IV implies 15.7x FY2026E sales \u2014 above market\n  [Aggregator \u2014 multiples.vc 13.6x current; estimate mine]. This is the\n  premium for the VAS mix.\n- Dividend yield 0.62% [Actual \u2014 pack]; buyback yield ~2.3% [Actual \u2014 pack].\n- PEG: 1.71 trailing [Aggregator \u2014 pack]; my IV \u2192 forward P/E 31.3 / 15.6 =\n  2.0 on FY2027E growth \u2014 higher than the historical 1.5\u20131.8 range.\nConclusion: my DCF is at the generous end of the multiple range \u2014 the market\nis paying ~13.6x EV/S, I am valuing ~15.7x EV/S on the same year. This\nexplains why MoS is only 13%.\n\n3-5. Tornado (top-3 variables, \u00b11\u03c3):\n1. WACC (8.0% \u2194 9.2%, i.e., 10Y 4.2% \u2194 5.2%): IV $753 \u2194 $616\n2. Terminal growth (3.5% \u2194 4.5%): IV $617 \u2194 $731\n3. Revenue CAGR (10-yr 10% \u2194 12%): IV ~$640 \u2194 ~$705\nTop-3 Thesis KPIs = 10Y yield, VAS growth, blended revenue growth.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS  [Layer 3.5]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1. Competitive response: if MA's VAS grows 20%+, Visa will deploy\naggressive VAS M&A and pricing (\u22121); fintechs (Stripe, Adyen, Block) compete\non the edge but lack MA's issuer relationships. Net \u22121.\n3.5-2. Reflexivity: positive \u2014 high stock price funds SBC ($0.6B/yr) and\nattracts talent; negative in a crash \u2014 banks may hedge exposure to a \"critical\ninfrastructure\" vendor. Reflexivity is modest but real.\n3.5-3. Customer behavior: early adopters (e-wallets: 24.9% of market 2025)\nalready shifted; MA's network is now the default rails UNDER the wallets.\nLTV/CAC for